id: H11
target: src/sello/private/sha512.nim
desc: finish: buffer-fill boundary comparison flip, 'if ctx.fill > 112:' -> 'if ctx.fill >= 112:', changing whether a message whose padded fill lands EXACTLY at 112 (no room for the 0x80 byte plus an 8-byte length half, but exactly enough for the 0x80 byte alone) takes the two-block finalization path -- flips behavior precisely at fill == 112, one of the exact padding-boundary edges (RFC-006 slice 1's 111/112/127/128 boundary lengths) CAVP vector lengths alone are not guaranteed to hit. The RFC-006 slice 4 list's named buffer-fill boundary-flip mutant.
====OLD====
  if ctx.fill > 112:
====NEW====
  if ctx.fill >= 112:
====END====
